1
00:00:03,910 --> 00:00:05,130
The math is all there.

2
00:00:05,130 --> 00:00:06,910
- It's not real. - Yes, it is.

3
00:00:06,910 --> 00:00:08,240
Yeah... uh, look.

4
00:00:08,240 --> 00:00:10,240
It is scientifically impossible

5
00:00:10,240 --> 00:00:12,140
for a person to tip a cow.

6
00:00:13,450 --> 00:00:16,110
Even you, with your stocky build and lumberjack shoulders,

7
00:00:16,110 --> 00:00:17,500
you couldn't do it.

8
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:20,210
It's horrible. Why would you push a cow over?

9
00:00:20,210 --> 00:00:21,240
They're sacred.

10
00:00:21,240 --> 00:00:22,090
Oh, stop it.

11
00:00:22,090 --> 00:00:24,200
I've seen you eat, like, a million hamburgers.

12
00:00:24,200 --> 00:00:27,580
Hey, an animal can be both sacred and delicious.

13
00:00:28,130 --> 00:00:29,670
Look, I'm telling you I've done it, okay?

14
00:00:29,670 --> 00:00:31,860
I clearly remember the cow standing up

15
00:00:31,860 --> 00:00:33,350
and then the cow on its side.

16
00:00:33,350 --> 00:00:35,270
Were you drunk?

17
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:38,460
I was 16 in Nebraska. What do you think?

18
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:41,490
I think you're the one who fell over.

19
00:00:42,540 --> 00:00:45,430
That would explain why the sky was also on its side.

20
00:00:47,790 --> 00:00:50,110
Howard. Cow tipping: real or not?

21
00:00:50,700 --> 00:00:52,620
I'm gonna say... not.

22
00:00:53,070 --> 00:00:54,900
That's just based on me trying to roll my mom over

23
00:00:54,900 --> 00:00:56,730
when she's snoring.

24
00:00:58,350 --> 00:01:00,480
Speaking of that big side of beef,

25
00:01:00,480 --> 00:01:04,340
uh, she's invited all of you to Thanksgiving at her house.

26
00:01:07,110 --> 00:01:09,010
You know, I've been told that a bald refusal

27
00:01:09,010 --> 00:01:10,650
of an invitation is rude

28
00:01:10,650 --> 00:01:13,070
and one must instead offer up a polite excuse, so...

29
00:01:13,070 --> 00:01:15,950
I'd love to go, but, unfortunately,

30
00:01:15,950 --> 00:01:17,700
that sounds awful.

31
00:01:20,770 --> 00:01:22,630
Come on, it'll be fun.

32
00:01:22,630 --> 00:01:24,270
Uh, we were actually gonna do it here.

33
00:01:24,270 --> 00:01:25,710
Please? Bernadette's bringing her dad

34
00:01:25,710 --> 00:01:26,760
'cause her mom's out of town,

35
00:01:26,760 --> 00:01:28,810
and I never have anything to say to that guy.

36
00:01:28,810 --> 00:01:31,080
Oh, since you put it that way, I'd love to go,

37
00:01:31,080 --> 00:01:33,200
but that sounds even more awful.

38
00:01:34,380 --> 00:01:35,450
It'd actually be nice to not hear

39
00:01:35,450 --> 00:01:37,480
Sheldon complain about my cooking all day.

40
00:01:37,480 --> 00:01:39,200
Yo... uh, excuse me,

41
00:01:39,200 --> 00:01:41,720
but every year you prepare a terrible meal

42
00:01:41,720 --> 00:01:43,750
and every year I criticize it.

43
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:46,550
Do our traditions mean nothing to you?

44
00:01:48,570 --> 00:01:50,000
- I want to go. - Yeah, me, too.

45
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:51,460
- I'm in. - Sheldon.

46
00:01:51,460 --> 00:01:54,030
Ugh, fine, I'll go.

47
00:01:54,030 --> 00:01:56,280
But if her food is delicious, Thanksgiving is ruined,

48
00:01:56,280 --> 00:01:57,690
and it's on you.

49
00:02:25,220 --> 00:02:27,970
Do we really have to go to Mrs. Wolowitz's house?

50
00:02:27,970 --> 00:02:29,120
We do.

51
00:02:29,120 --> 00:02:31,660
And I expect you to be on your best behavior.

52
00:02:32,610 --> 00:02:35,430
Now I know how the African slaves felt.

53
00:02:37,030 --> 00:02:38,520
Being dragged from their homes

54
00:02:38,520 --> 00:02:41,320
to labor under the yoke of the white man.

55
00:02:42,530 --> 00:02:44,100
Are you honestly comparing

56
00:02:44,100 --> 00:02:46,340
Thanksgiving dinner at Wolowitz's mom's

57
00:02:46,340 --> 00:02:47,810
with one of the greatest tragedies

58
00:02:47,810 --> 00:02:50,050
in the history of mankind?

59
00:02:50,050 --> 00:02:51,810
Yes.

60
00:02:52,940 --> 00:02:54,880
Sheldon, you can have a nice Thanksgiving anywhere.

61
00:02:54,880 --> 00:02:56,430
I spent one in Vegas.

62
00:02:56,430 --> 00:02:57,260
You did?

63
00:02:57,260 --> 00:02:58,900
Yeah, back when I was dating Zack.

64
00:02:58,900 --> 00:03:00,670
It was actually more fun than I thought.

65
00:03:00,670 --> 00:03:03,490
We gambled, we went to one of those cheesy wedding chapels,

66
00:03:03,490 --> 00:03:04,840
we had a really good turkey dinner.

67
00:03:04,840 --> 00:03:07,400
Which was surprising, since we were at a strip club.

68
00:03:09,680 --> 00:03:10,990
Wait, you went to a chapel?

69
00:03:10,990 --> 00:03:12,540
- Yeah. - Why?

70
00:03:12,540 --> 00:03:15,010
We had one of those silly fake weddings.

71
00:03:19,780 --> 00:03:21,070
Penny...

72
00:03:21,070 --> 00:03:22,810
you know those are real, right?

73
00:03:22,810 --> 00:03:24,600
No, they're not.

74
00:03:25,820 --> 00:03:27,490
Yeah, they are.

75
00:03:28,430 --> 00:03:30,110
No, they're not.

76
00:03:30,980 --> 00:03:32,030
Yeah, they are.

77
00:03:32,030 --> 00:03:33,950
- He's right. - They're real.

78
00:03:34,890 --> 00:03:37,570
But it... didn't seem real.

79
00:03:39,010 --> 00:03:40,280
Let me ask you a question.

80
00:03:40,280 --> 00:03:44,750
At any point, was Las Vegas on its side?

81
00:03:49,710 --> 00:03:51,690
- Hi, Dad. - Hi, honey.

82
00:03:53,130 --> 00:03:55,140
Oh, you brought beer for everybody.

83
00:03:55,880 --> 00:03:58,910
Uh, okay, yeah, it's for everybody.

84
00:04:01,520 --> 00:04:04,150
I really just wanted to have a nice, quiet day at home

85
00:04:04,150 --> 00:04:05,530
and watch the game.

86
00:04:05,530 --> 00:04:07,970
You can have a quiet day and watch the game here.

87
00:04:07,970 --> 00:04:11,730
Howard, the medicine's not working!

88
00:04:13,280 --> 00:04:14,530
You just took it.

89
00:04:14,530 --> 00:04:17,730
At least let it reach your first stomach!

90
00:04:21,240 --> 00:04:22,730
Hey, Mike.

91
00:04:22,730 --> 00:04:24,880
- Let me help you out, there. - Thanks.

92
00:04:24,880 --> 00:04:26,280
What's wrong with your mom?

93
00:04:26,280 --> 00:04:27,630
Oh, her gout's flaring up.

94
00:04:27,630 --> 00:04:29,070
Turns out an apple pie a day

95
00:04:29,070 --> 00:04:31,040
does not keep the doctor away.

96
00:04:31,960 --> 00:04:35,570
How can one little toe hurt so bad?

97
00:04:35,570 --> 00:04:37,330
Maybe because that little piggy

98
00:04:37,330 --> 00:04:39,760
is being crushed by the barn!

99
00:04:42,390 --> 00:04:43,820
She should quiet down soon.

100
00:04:43,820 --> 00:04:45,640
I gave her enough pain meds to choke a...

101
00:04:45,640 --> 00:04:47,360
well, her.

102
00:04:49,660 --> 00:04:51,560
I guess we're gonna have to do all the cooking.

103
00:04:51,560 --> 00:04:52,500
I have a better idea.

104
00:04:52,500 --> 00:04:54,610
If you think you're gonna make me do all this by myself,

105
00:04:54,610 --> 00:04:55,510
you're crazy.

106
00:04:55,510 --> 00:04:57,160
I was gonna make Raj do it all by himself.

107
00:04:57,160 --> 00:04:59,090
Oh, well, that's a great idea.

108
00:05:02,320 --> 00:05:04,150
No traffic, we're sailing.

109
00:05:04,150 --> 00:05:04,920
Yes.

110
00:05:04,920 --> 00:05:06,870
Like we're on a ship.

111
00:05:08,130 --> 00:05:10,740
Coming from Africa to America.

112
00:05:12,680 --> 00:05:15,230
Sheldon, that's completely inappropriate.

113
00:05:15,230 --> 00:05:18,590
You can't keep comparing yourself to a slave.

114
00:05:19,370 --> 00:05:21,150
Yes, Miss Amy.

115
00:05:24,300 --> 00:05:26,540
I can't believe you're married to that idiot.

116
00:05:26,540 --> 00:05:28,690
Ugh, would you stop? We just did it as a goof.

117
00:05:28,690 --> 00:05:30,340
Well, a goof or not, you're actually married.

118
00:05:30,340 --> 00:05:32,300
- You need to get this taken care of. - I will.

119
00:05:32,300 --> 00:05:34,600
Why are you making this such a big deal?

120
00:05:34,600 --> 00:05:36,090
Oh, oh, oh, I have a reason.

121
00:05:36,090 --> 00:05:39,200
It could be because you said yes to marrying Zack,

122
00:05:39,200 --> 00:05:40,760
but every time Leonard's proposed,

123
00:05:40,760 --> 00:05:42,940
he's gotten a resounding no.

124
00:05:44,720 --> 00:05:46,740
Yeah, that's just off the top of my head.

125
00:05:47,950 --> 00:05:49,420
So how do I undo this?

126
00:05:49,420 --> 00:05:51,000
I'm hoping you can get an annulment.

127
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:52,390
It's just like it never happened.

128
00:05:52,390 --> 00:05:54,020
Great, well, what do I have to do?

129
00:05:54,020 --> 00:05:55,560
It says here you can get an annulment

130
00:05:55,560 --> 00:05:57,500
if any of the following conditions are met.

131
00:05:57,500 --> 00:05:59,860
"Were you unable to consummate the marriage?"

132
00:06:00,160 --> 00:06:01,990
Penny? Next.

133
00:06:03,460 --> 00:06:06,000
"Is there any evidence of fraud, bigamy,

134
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:07,680
want of understanding?"

135
00:06:07,680 --> 00:06:09,680
"Want of understanding?" What does that even mean?

136
00:06:09,680 --> 00:06:12,160
Ding, ding, ding. We have a winner.

137
00:06:14,200 --> 00:06:15,580
Thanks for saving the day.

138
00:06:15,580 --> 00:06:16,600
Ah, no problem.

139
00:06:16,600 --> 00:06:17,650
It wouldn't be Thanksgiving

140
00:06:17,650 --> 00:06:20,360
without an Indian providing the food.

141
00:06:23,040 --> 00:06:25,100
Uh, now, where does your mom keep the Crisco?

142
00:06:25,100 --> 00:06:25,930
Um, I don't know.

143
00:06:25,930 --> 00:06:28,080
Probably in a wad in her cheek.

144
00:06:29,630 --> 00:06:30,520
I'll help Raj in here.

145
00:06:30,520 --> 00:06:32,270
Why don't you go keep my dad company?

146
00:06:32,270 --> 00:06:33,490
Oh, he doesn't want me in there.

147
00:06:33,490 --> 00:06:36,730
I'm the creepy little guy who has sex with his daughter.

148
00:06:39,290 --> 00:06:41,970
- Don't be silly, he loves you. - Does he?

149
00:06:41,970 --> 00:06:44,430
- Okay, he cares about you a lot. - Really?

150
00:06:44,430 --> 00:06:46,720
I do crap for you all the time. Get out there.

151
00:06:53,270 --> 00:06:56,530
So your wife's in Arizona with the grandkids?

152
00:07:00,660 --> 00:07:03,000
You know, my mom's been to...Arizona.

153
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:06,180
She rode one of those mules down in the Grand Canyon.

154
00:07:06,180 --> 00:07:08,450
Long story short, they had to shoot it.

155
00:07:12,870 --> 00:07:15,370
'Cause she's so fat.

156
00:07:19,290 --> 00:07:22,290
I'll get the door while you finish laughing.

157
00:07:25,390 --> 00:07:26,420
Hey, guys.

158
00:07:26,420 --> 00:07:27,630
Happy Thanksgiving.

159
00:07:27,630 --> 00:07:29,240
It smells wonderful.

160
00:07:29,240 --> 00:07:31,550
Is anyone slaving away in the kitchen?

161
00:07:31,550 --> 00:07:32,990
- Because I, too, know... - Sheldon.

162
00:07:35,040 --> 00:07:36,750
Here. Thank you for having us.

163
00:07:37,390 --> 00:07:39,040
- What's with you? - Oh, she's mad at me

164
00:07:39,040 --> 00:07:41,900
because she just found out she's married to Zack.

165
00:07:41,900 --> 00:07:42,670
Really?

166
00:07:42,670 --> 00:07:44,750
That dumb-ass she used to date?

167
00:07:44,750 --> 00:07:46,940
That's hysterical.

168
00:07:48,130 --> 00:07:50,930
I can't believe I felt bad for opening this in the car.

169
00:07:56,770 --> 00:07:58,020
- You need any help? - Uh, yeah,

170
00:07:58,020 --> 00:08:00,240
can you, uh, reach that, uh, gravy boat up there?

171
00:08:00,240 --> 00:08:01,710
- Uh, sure. - Great.

172
00:08:01,710 --> 00:08:03,580
That makes one of you.

173
00:08:06,340 --> 00:08:08,690
Okay, we have a lot to do and not much time to do it.

174
00:08:08,690 --> 00:08:11,130
Bernadette, you're on corn, gravy and yam detail.

175
00:08:11,130 --> 00:08:12,670
Amy, you're on rolls, cranberries

176
00:08:12,670 --> 00:08:15,400
and making sure Bernadette stays away from the marshmallows.

177
00:08:16,510 --> 00:08:18,250
That's right, I see you.

178
00:08:20,100 --> 00:08:21,030
Okay, if you have any questions,

179
00:08:21,030 --> 00:08:22,830
I'll be over here basting my ass off.

180
00:08:22,830 --> 00:08:24,900
Focus is key.

181
00:08:24,900 --> 00:08:28,220
Did you guys know Penny married Zack three years ago?

182
00:08:28,220 --> 00:08:29,970
- What? - Wha...?

183
00:08:35,450 --> 00:08:37,070
You ever play football?

184
00:08:37,070 --> 00:08:38,830
A little in college.

185
00:08:38,830 --> 00:08:40,450
- You? - No.

186
00:08:40,520 --> 00:08:43,510
But I did get tackled in the hallway once.

187
00:08:45,330 --> 00:08:47,420
The whole school cheered.

188
00:08:50,920 --> 00:08:52,740
Hey, I found the, uh, court papers

189
00:08:52,740 --> 00:08:53,840
that you and Zack need to fill out.

190
00:08:53,840 --> 00:08:55,600
- I'll print them when we get home. - Fine.

191
00:08:55,600 --> 00:08:57,630
And we can just put this whole thing behind us.

192
00:08:57,630 --> 00:08:59,270
- Are you done? - What?

193
00:08:59,270 --> 00:09:00,480
Look, I get it, I screwed up.

194
00:09:00,480 --> 00:09:02,020
Is this all we're gonna talk about the rest of the day?

195
00:09:02,020 --> 00:09:03,220
Why are you mad at me?

196
00:09:03,220 --> 00:09:04,380
You're the one that did the stupid thing.

197
00:09:04,380 --> 00:09:05,520
I'm just trying to fix it.

198
00:09:05,970 --> 00:09:07,270
I need some air.

199
00:09:07,270 --> 00:09:09,160
Well... Penny.

200
00:09:09,610 --> 00:09:11,330
Now, I don't know the first thing about women,

201
00:09:11,330 --> 00:09:13,420
but I would not follow her.

202
00:09:16,220 --> 00:09:17,900
Listen to Stretch.

203
00:09:24,650 --> 00:09:26,100
How am I the bad guy?

204
00:09:26,100 --> 00:09:28,880
She's the one who married someone else. I'm the victim.

205
00:09:28,880 --> 00:09:30,060
Sounds like Zack's the victim.

206
00:09:30,060 --> 00:09:31,820
You're sleeping with his wife.

207
00:09:34,810 --> 00:09:37,690
I've kept my marriage together for 35 years.

208
00:09:37,690 --> 00:09:39,330
Can I weigh in here?

209
00:09:39,330 --> 00:09:40,250
Sure.

210
00:09:40,250 --> 00:09:42,670
I'm trying to watch the game. Shut up.

211
00:09:45,700 --> 00:09:48,240
How do you not make a first down there?

212
00:09:48,240 --> 00:09:50,270
They passed against a nickel defense.

213
00:09:50,270 --> 00:09:52,150
They should have run it off-tackle.

214
00:09:54,900 --> 00:09:56,610
How the hell do you know that?

215
00:09:56,610 --> 00:09:58,290
My father loved football.

216
00:09:58,290 --> 00:09:59,590
He always made me watch it

217
00:09:59,590 --> 00:10:02,110
before I was allowed to do my homework.

218
00:10:03,260 --> 00:10:05,120
Well, you'll be happy to know I just spoke to Zack

219
00:10:05,120 --> 00:10:06,830
and he's willing to sign the court papers.

220
00:10:06,830 --> 00:10:08,180
He's on his way here now.

221
00:10:08,180 --> 00:10:10,820
- Wait, you invited him here? - Yeah.

222
00:10:10,820 --> 00:10:12,730
I'm getting ready to weigh in again.

223
00:10:12,730 --> 00:10:13,310
Come on.

224
00:10:15,620 --> 00:10:17,970
What do you think they ought to do now?

225
00:10:18,320 --> 00:10:20,210
I would throw a quick slant to a wideout,

226
00:10:20,210 --> 00:10:22,290
given that the defense is showing blitz.

227
00:10:22,290 --> 00:10:23,850
Oh, I love a good blitz,

228
00:10:23,850 --> 00:10:26,160
especially with sour cream.

229
00:10:29,680 --> 00:10:30,450
Get it?

230
00:10:30,450 --> 00:10:32,960
'Cause it sounds like "Blintz."

231
00:10:33,880 --> 00:10:35,750
Did someone say "Blintz"?!

232
00:10:37,400 --> 00:10:39,770
I just don't understand why you invited him here today.

233
00:10:39,770 --> 00:10:41,490
Because you wouldn't shut up about it.

234
00:10:41,490 --> 00:10:42,780
When I called him, he had nothing to do,

235
00:10:42,780 --> 00:10:43,770
so I just thought it would...

236
00:10:43,770 --> 00:10:45,350
Hey, guys, I'm trying to cook in here.

237
00:10:45,350 --> 00:10:46,560
Oh, sorry. We'll keep it down.

238
00:10:46,560 --> 00:10:47,990
No, no, speak up.

239
00:10:49,610 --> 00:10:50,620
I'm about to use the blender,

240
00:10:50,620 --> 00:10:52,330
and I don't want to miss anything.

241
00:10:53,880 --> 00:10:55,400
Well, you might have to cook for one more

242
00:10:55,400 --> 00:10:56,960
because she invited Zack.

243
00:10:56,960 --> 00:10:58,640
- What? - Ooh!

244
00:11:00,030 --> 00:11:01,370
My, my.

245
00:11:01,370 --> 00:11:05,130
The plot, like my gravy, thickens.

246
00:11:09,700 --> 00:11:12,110
I don't care for your mother's bathroom.

247
00:11:12,110 --> 00:11:13,930
There's not an angle to do one's business

248
00:11:13,930 --> 00:11:16,770
without a clown figurine staring at you.

249
00:11:18,240 --> 00:11:19,530
That's why I sit.

250
00:11:19,530 --> 00:11:22,360
Yeah, that's why.

251
00:11:25,510 --> 00:11:27,410
You remember the Thanksgiving game

252
00:11:27,410 --> 00:11:29,400
when it snowed in Dallas?

253
00:11:29,400 --> 00:11:30,850
1993--

254
00:11:30,850 --> 00:11:32,900
Leon Lett blew the game in the final seconds

255
00:11:32,900 --> 00:11:34,940
and the Dolphins emerged victorious.

256
00:11:34,940 --> 00:11:37,170
Then I finally got to do my calculus.

257
00:11:38,420 --> 00:11:41,310
I was so pissed, I wanted to shoot my TV.

258
00:11:41,310 --> 00:11:42,830
So was my dad.

259
00:11:42,830 --> 00:11:44,510
And then he did.

260
00:11:46,550 --> 00:11:47,590
- Anyone need a beer?-  Yeah.

261
00:11:48,210 --> 00:11:49,610
Thank God.

262
00:11:51,090 --> 00:11:53,750
So, does your dad still live in Texas?

263
00:11:53,750 --> 00:11:56,800
No. He died when I was 14.

264
00:11:57,560 --> 00:11:59,200
I'm sorry to hear that.

265
00:11:59,200 --> 00:12:01,880
So was the man who owned the local liquor store.

266
00:12:03,550 --> 00:12:06,050
He cried and cried.

267
00:12:07,270 --> 00:12:08,310
Here you go.

268
00:12:08,310 --> 00:12:09,900
Oh, thanks.

269
00:12:10,560 --> 00:12:13,190
So, if your dad died when you were 14,

270
00:12:13,190 --> 00:12:16,280
you were never old enough to have a beer with the man.

271
00:12:16,280 --> 00:12:17,520
No, sir.

272
00:12:17,520 --> 00:12:20,260
He did try to give me one for my high school graduation,

273
00:12:20,260 --> 00:12:23,240
but I was 11 and my mom said no.

274
00:12:28,120 --> 00:12:30,350
Well, you're having one with me.

275
00:12:35,080 --> 00:12:36,410
All right.

276
00:12:38,740 --> 00:12:40,260
To your dad.

277
00:12:43,950 --> 00:12:47,250
I never had a beer with my dad, either.

278
00:12:51,070 --> 00:12:53,500
Do you mind? We're having a moment here.

279
00:13:01,470 --> 00:13:03,490
I can't believe Penny's married to Zack.

280
00:13:03,860 --> 00:13:05,550
Wonder what she saw in that guy.

281
00:13:05,550 --> 00:13:06,300
I don't know.

282
00:13:06,300 --> 00:13:08,880
He's sweet, he's tall, handsome.

283
00:13:08,880 --> 00:13:10,740
Broad shoulders, good hair.

284
00:13:11,200 --> 00:13:13,050
Wonder what she sees in Leonard.

285
00:13:16,870 --> 00:13:18,180
How's it going out there?

286
00:13:18,180 --> 00:13:20,110
Sheldon and your dad are bonding

287
00:13:20,110 --> 00:13:21,950
and completely ignoring me.

288
00:13:21,950 --> 00:13:23,530
I know how you feel.

289
00:13:23,530 --> 00:13:27,140
Sheldon ignored me for a week when he got that Roomba vacuum.

290
00:13:29,270 --> 00:13:31,320
I kick it when he's not looking.

291
00:13:33,540 --> 00:13:34,880
What are they doing?

292
00:13:34,880 --> 00:13:37,570
They're drinking beer and watching football.

293
00:13:37,570 --> 00:13:39,050
So why don't do that with them.

294
00:13:39,050 --> 00:13:40,600
They don't want me.

295
00:13:40,600 --> 00:13:41,540
What do you mean?

296
00:13:41,540 --> 00:13:45,140
Well, Sheldon started talking about how his dad isn't alive anymore,

297
00:13:45,140 --> 00:13:47,000
and they were toasting, and I tried to tell them about

298
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:49,120
how sad I was when my dad abandoned...

299
00:13:49,120 --> 00:13:50,320
Zack's here!

300
00:13:51,190 --> 00:13:52,690
Stir the gravy.

301
00:13:55,900 --> 00:13:57,660
Sorry. I really want to hear how sad you are.

302
00:13:57,660 --> 00:13:59,500
I'll be back in like five, ten minutes.

303
00:14:04,690 --> 00:14:06,960
Sorry she made you come over here on a holiday.

304
00:14:06,960 --> 00:14:08,880
It's all right. I didn't have anything going on.

305
00:14:08,880 --> 00:14:10,240
Plus, Penny told me we're married,

306
00:14:10,240 --> 00:14:12,880
and Thanksgiving's a time to be with family.

307
00:14:14,530 --> 00:14:15,200
Yeah, okay, great.

308
00:14:15,200 --> 00:14:16,240
Can we just get this over with?

309
00:14:16,240 --> 00:14:19,330
Yeah, uh, you guys have to sign here and here.

310
00:14:19,330 --> 00:14:21,090
On Monday, we'll file for the annulment,

311
00:14:21,090 --> 00:14:22,960
and this "Marriage" will be over.

312
00:14:22,960 --> 00:14:23,340
Okay.

313
00:14:25,200 --> 00:14:26,930
I don't know if I want to sign it.

314
00:14:30,840 --> 00:14:32,240
Why won't you sign it?

315
00:14:32,240 --> 00:14:35,110
I just think splitting up can be rough on kids.

316
00:14:36,720 --> 00:14:38,050
We don't have any kids.

317
00:14:38,050 --> 00:14:39,590
Are you sure? 'Cause you didn't know

318
00:14:39,590 --> 00:14:41,740
we were married until this morning.

319
00:14:43,970 --> 00:14:45,190
Okay, look, Zack, come on.

320
00:14:45,190 --> 00:14:47,290
You know neither of us thought this was real.

321
00:14:47,290 --> 00:14:49,740
I mean, we were married by an Elvis impersonator.

322
00:14:49,740 --> 00:14:51,450
Of course it was an impersonator.

323
00:14:51,450 --> 00:14:53,790
We could never afford a real Elvis.

324
00:14:57,010 --> 00:14:59,260
You married him instead of me?

325
00:14:59,260 --> 00:15:01,020
Good call.

326
00:15:01,880 --> 00:15:02,670
Sign the papers.

327
00:15:02,670 --> 00:15:04,050
Hang on. You know what?

328
00:15:04,050 --> 00:15:05,860
You have been a jerk about this all day.

329
00:15:05,860 --> 00:15:07,300
You always do this-- whenever I mess up,

330
00:15:07,300 --> 00:15:09,200
you're right there to make me feel even worse about it.

331
00:15:09,200 --> 00:15:10,050
That is not true.

332
00:15:10,050 --> 00:15:12,000
Yeah, we could've waited till Monday, signed the papers,

333
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:12,970
this all would have been over.

334
00:15:12,970 --> 00:15:14,090
You're the one who invited him here.

335
00:15:14,090 --> 00:15:15,160
Oh, there you go again--

336
00:15:15,160 --> 00:15:17,340
just another mistake you're throwing in my face.

337
00:15:17,340 --> 00:15:19,230
Not cool, bro.

338
00:15:21,560 --> 00:15:22,410
I'm starting to think

339
00:15:22,410 --> 00:15:25,070
you're not the kind of guy I want dating my wife.

340
00:15:28,050 --> 00:15:28,530
Yeah, well,

341
00:15:28,530 --> 00:15:30,440
she's not gonna be your wife for long.

342
00:15:30,440 --> 00:15:32,180
Oh, no. Are you dying?

343
00:15:34,040 --> 00:15:35,890
I'm about to. Sign the paper.

344
00:15:38,140 --> 00:15:40,110
Know what they say: "Happy wife,

345
00:15:40,110 --> 00:15:42,250
happy life."

346
00:15:43,290 --> 00:15:44,420
Let's eat.

347
00:15:48,210 --> 00:15:52,540
Two, three, eight, four, six.

348
00:15:56,190 --> 00:15:58,000
That's all I can do without throwing up.

349
00:15:59,260 --> 00:16:00,910
That is not what I expected

350
00:16:00,910 --> 00:16:03,760
when you said you were gonna burp "Pie."

351
00:16:04,900 --> 00:16:07,300
Did somebody say "Pie"?!

352
00:16:09,200 --> 00:16:10,760
I don't know what's scarier:

353
00:16:10,760 --> 00:16:12,180
the bathroom clowns

354
00:16:12,180 --> 00:16:14,170
or the woman that put them there.

355
00:16:15,660 --> 00:16:19,140
All I know is you can only fit one of her in a car.

356
00:16:22,510 --> 00:16:24,810
And there's the clown that came out of her.

357
00:16:29,830 --> 00:16:32,030
I really didn't want to come here,

358
00:16:32,430 --> 00:16:33,550
but this is shaping up to be

359
00:16:33,550 --> 00:16:36,390
one of the best Thanksgivings I've had in a long time.

360
00:16:36,390 --> 00:16:37,580
Me, too.

361
00:16:38,790 --> 00:16:41,440
Hey. Howie says you've been making fun of him all day!

362
00:16:41,440 --> 00:16:44,080
Now, both of you apologize right now!

363
00:16:45,110 --> 00:16:47,100
She's so tiny.

364
00:16:51,400 --> 00:16:53,540
It's funny when she's mad.

365
00:16:56,570 --> 00:16:57,880
All right, mister,

366
00:16:57,880 --> 00:17:00,740
I think you owe Howard and Bernadette an apology.

367
00:17:02,370 --> 00:17:03,760
Perhaps you're right.

368
00:17:06,410 --> 00:17:08,150
I'm sorry for my behavior.

369
00:17:08,150 --> 00:17:11,390
I've had alcohol, and it's caused me to be inappropriate.

370
00:17:11,910 --> 00:17:13,110
- It's okay. - Don't worry about it.

371
00:17:13,110 --> 00:17:14,550
Thank you.

372
00:17:15,420 --> 00:17:16,690
Ain't she great?

373
00:17:17,650 --> 00:17:19,100
Sheldon.

374
00:17:19,100 --> 00:17:21,380
Now, how's about you get us a couple of beers?

375
00:17:34,810 --> 00:17:36,240
Thanks again for cooking.

376
00:17:36,240 --> 00:17:37,600
Yeah, everything was delicious.

377
00:17:37,600 --> 00:17:41,020
Well, I couldn't have done it without my two favorite girls.

378
00:17:41,610 --> 00:17:44,240
Martha Stewart and Rachael Ray.

379
00:17:48,470 --> 00:17:50,610
Hey, Sheldon, what do you say we go outside

380
00:17:50,610 --> 00:17:52,950
and throw around the old pigskin?

381
00:17:53,380 --> 00:17:55,230
This is a Jewish house.

382
00:17:55,230 --> 00:17:57,410
I don't think they have pigskin.

383
00:17:59,790 --> 00:18:02,560
Did someone say pigskin!

384
00:18:04,780 --> 00:18:06,340
Hey, honey, I'm sorry about today.

385
00:18:06,340 --> 00:18:08,040
And I promise, next time I get married,

386
00:18:08,040 --> 00:18:09,490
it won't be a joke.

387
00:18:09,490 --> 00:18:11,350
It'll be for love.

388
00:18:11,350 --> 00:18:12,980
Or money.

389
00:18:16,310 --> 00:18:17,540
I'm sorry, too.

390
00:18:18,160 --> 00:18:19,070
Don't be.

391
00:18:19,070 --> 00:18:20,100
It's my fault.

392
00:18:20,100 --> 00:18:21,550
I was a terrible husband.

393
00:18:23,530 --> 00:18:25,090
I was never around.

394
00:18:27,890 --> 00:18:29,580
I know I'm hard on you,

395
00:18:29,580 --> 00:18:32,480
but you're not the worst son-in-law in the world.

396
00:18:32,480 --> 00:18:35,910
Mike, that's the nicest thing you've ever said to me.

397
00:18:35,910 --> 00:18:38,130
Well, I'm drunk.

398
00:18:41,720 --> 00:18:44,580
I just vomited on a lot of clowns.

